    "summary": "Woman&#039;s reversible coat with elbow-length sleeves, known as jillāyeh, made of  indigo-dyed cotton with taffeta (heremzi) appliqué patches in red, yellow and  green as well as ikat and &#039;atlas&#039; satin appliqué patches along the front and on the sleeves. The back is richly embroidered on the inside mostly in cross-stitch with  multicoloured silks.  The coat is reversible and could be worn inside- out, the inner lapels embroidered in cross-stitch in red and white.    The coat has a yoke and under-arm inserts of blue cotton.",
